<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qadmus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Al-Qadmus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qadmus is a town in the coastal mountains of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tartus">Tartus</a> governorate, built around a medieval castle. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nizari-ismaili-state">Nizari Ismailis</a> acquired the castle in 1132, the first of the fortresses they gained in the mountains of the Jabal Bahra, and it remained one of their strongholds until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> took their castles in the early 1270s. It is still a centre of Syria's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> community.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qadmus.jpg" alt="Qadmus" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ACEsAF · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al_Qadmus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
